# No AI attribution in git

When writing commit messages, PR titles, or PR bodies:

- Do **not** mention Cursor, Copilot, ChatGPT, Claude, or any AI assistant
- Do **not** add trailers or footers like "Collaborated by Cursor", "Generated by AI", "Co-authored-by: Cursor", or similar
- Write commits as normal project history: what changed and why, in the repo's existing style

If the environment auto-appends `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`, strip it before push (e.g. rewrite the tip commit with `git commit-tree` so the published message has no AI trailer). Never leave that trailer on `main`.
